Maybe you should try and get some sleep.

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:25.559
No.

00:16:25.559 --> 00:16:26.639
I'll be fine.

00:16:26.639 --> 00:16:28.720
OK.

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:29.399
Well.

00:16:29.399 --> 00:16:33.819
Um, I brought you your homework.

00:16:33.819 --> 00:16:36.259
Mr. Blair said that you could make up your history exam

00:16:36.259 --> 00:16:37.720
as long as you have a note from your parents.

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:41.120
You're the best.

00:16:49.399 --> 00:16:50.899
Can I tell you something?

00:16:50.899 --> 00:16:51.799
Sure.

00:16:54.519 --> 00:16:57.259
I had this dream, and it's really freaking me out.

00:16:57.259 --> 00:16:58.059
What was it about?

00:16:58.059 --> 00:16:59.000
A lot of things.

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:01.360
This girl.

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:03.419
Oh.

00:17:03.419 --> 00:17:05.880
No, Lana, it's not like that.

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:08.220
She needed help.

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:09.319
Let me guess.

00:17:09.319 --> 00:17:10.680
You had to save her.

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:12.619
Except I couldn't.

00:17:12.619 --> 00:17:15.319
Her name's Sarah, and she moved into your old house.

00:17:15.319 --> 00:17:16.519
When did you meet her?

00:17:16.519 --> 00:17:17.180
That's the thing.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:19.019
I haven't.

00:17:19.019 --> 00:17:20.180
How could I be dreaming about her?

00:17:23.119 --> 00:17:24.819
Well, maybe if you walked me through the dream,

00:17:24.819 --> 00:17:27.460
we could figure it out together.

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:28.420
You don't think I'm nuts?

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:30.779
No.

00:17:30.779 --> 00:17:33.120
Clark, I think you have a lot of issues,

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:35.060
but I do not think you have lost your mind.

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:40.380
OK, so where did you see her first?

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:42.340
Breda Lake.

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:43.720
You were there.

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:44.620
Really?

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:46.340
What were we doing?

00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:48.460
Nothing.

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:49.500
It's really hazy.

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:53.360
OK.

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:55.640
Well, I have a better idea.

00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:57.140
Why don't we go see Sarah in person?

00:17:57.140 --> 00:17:57.840
No.

00:17:57.839 --> 00:17:58.819
I'll tell little Carl at the car.

00:17:58.819 --> 00:17:59.339
OK.

00:18:09.879 --> 00:18:10.399
You know what.

00:18:10.399 --> 00:18:12.399
She seems so bad.

00:18:15.939 --> 00:18:18.699
Do the doctors think she'll come out of it?

00:18:18.699 --> 00:18:19.599
No.

00:18:19.599 --> 00:18:20.519
There's always hope.

00:18:24.599 --> 00:18:26.959
It must be really hard to see your daughter like this.

00:18:26.959 --> 00:18:27.240
Probably quite a lot.

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:27.399
Right.

00:18:27.399 --> 00:18:27.839
Yeah.

00:18:27.839 --> 00:18:29.839
Sarah's my niece.

00:18:29.839 --> 00:18:33.839
So, this is your old house, Lana.

00:18:33.839 --> 00:18:36.839
And you're the boyfriend next door.

00:18:36.839 --> 00:18:38.839
What exactly happened?

00:18:38.839 --> 00:18:39.839
Clark.

00:18:39.839 --> 00:18:41.839
It's okay. It's no secret.

00:18:41.839 --> 00:18:43.839
It was a car accident.

00:18:43.839 --> 00:18:48.839
Sarah and her parents went off the low bridge on their way home from a soccer game.

00:18:48.839 --> 00:18:53.839
Paramedics say Sarah was asleep, which is probably why she survived.

00:18:53.839 --> 00:18:54.839
Sarah's from Smallville?

00:18:54.839 --> 00:18:57.839
Granville. Just over the county line.

00:18:57.839 --> 00:19:00.839
Bilacs. Those are Sarah's favorite.

00:19:03.839 --> 00:19:04.839
Yes.

00:19:06.839 --> 00:19:08.839
How did you know that?

00:19:08.839 --> 00:19:11.839
They're my favorite, too.

00:19:11.839 --> 00:19:14.839
Must be kismet, living in the same house.

00:19:23.839 --> 00:19:24.839
That's an interesting medal.

00:19:24.839 --> 00:19:26.839
This?

00:19:26.839 --> 00:19:29.839
Well, it's just good old Saint Christopher.

00:19:29.839 --> 00:19:32.839
The patron saint of travelers, right?

00:19:32.839 --> 00:19:39.839
Yes. Yes, I say his prayer every night in the hopes that Sarah's journey will end and she'll come back to us.

00:19:41.839 --> 00:19:47.839
Look, I'm sorry. You'll have to excuse me. It's time for Sarah's medication.

00:19:48.839 --> 00:19:50.839
Thank you for stopping by.

00:19:54.839 --> 00:19:55.839
I'm sure you'll be all right.

00:19:55.839 --> 00:19:56.839
I'll be fine.

00:20:16.839 --> 00:20:20.839
Dad, I thought I made it clear that I'm back, fully committed to Luthor Corp and to you.

00:20:20.839 --> 00:20:22.839
And I'm delighted...

00:20:22.839 --> 00:20:24.839
Do you hear it?

00:20:28.839 --> 00:20:31.839
Now, what's the problem?

00:20:31.839 --> 00:20:35.839
I've been blocked out of half the computer files I need to do my job.

00:20:35.839 --> 00:20:37.839
Insufficient security clearance.

00:20:39.839 --> 00:20:41.839
Thank you, Milly.

00:20:44.839 --> 00:20:46.839
These, uh...

00:20:46.839 --> 00:20:52.839
Security measures, Lex, are a necessary evil. You should know that.

00:20:52.839 --> 00:20:54.839
We have to protect our assets.

00:20:54.839 --> 00:20:56.839
From me?

00:20:56.839 --> 00:20:59.839
I applaud your renewed commitment to Luther Corp.

00:20:59.839 --> 00:21:03.839
After what you've been through, it's remarkable.

00:21:03.839 --> 00:21:06.839
But you think I might betray you again.

00:21:08.839 --> 00:21:11.839
Betray me? That's an interesting notion.

00:21:12.839 --> 00:21:14.839
Might you?

00:21:16.839 --> 00:21:18.839
I want this to work.

00:21:20.839 --> 00:21:22.839
I want us to be a family again.

00:21:22.839 --> 00:21:24.839
You have nothing to fear from me.

00:21:26.839 --> 00:21:30.839
Why have you refused to complete the psychological profile?

00:21:30.839 --> 00:21:32.839
Come on, Dad.

00:21:32.839 --> 00:21:35.839
You've never believed in that psychobabble, and neither do I.

00:21:35.839 --> 00:21:38.839
I believe that, uh, personal, emotional problems...

00:21:38.839 --> 00:21:41.839
are bound to affect day-to-day decision-making.

00:21:41.839 --> 00:21:45.839
I think that dreams can often reveal hidden dangers...

00:21:46.839 --> 00:21:48.839
and that the world is in service of warning.

00:21:48.839 --> 00:21:50.839
Spare me the Jungian cliff notes, Dad.

00:21:50.839 --> 00:21:52.839
It's five sessions, Lex. That's all.

00:21:52.839 --> 00:21:55.839
I thought you wanted to reestablish our bond.

00:21:56.839 --> 00:21:58.839
I do.

00:21:58.839 --> 00:22:00.839
Then do it.

00:22:00.839 --> 00:22:03.839
Prove that my total confidence in you is justified.

00:22:09.839 --> 00:22:11.839
Clark Kent dreaming of the girl next door.

00:22:11.839 --> 00:22:13.839
Isn't it nice to know that some things never change?

00:22:13.839 --> 00:22:15.839
Right now, I'm just trying to stay awake.

00:22:15.839 --> 00:22:18.839
Yeah. Even Red Bull has its limits. Trust me.

00:22:18.839 --> 00:22:20.839
I've tested them.

00:22:20.839 --> 00:22:22.839
I think Sarah's reaching out to me for help.

00:22:22.839 --> 00:22:24.839
Entering your dreams to communicate?

00:22:24.839 --> 00:22:26.839
How else would I know these details of her life?

00:22:26.839 --> 00:22:28.839
Like the lilacs?

00:22:28.839 --> 00:22:32.839
There is a theory that telepathic receptivity is increased during REM sleep.

00:22:32.839 --> 00:22:34.839
It has to do with frontal lobe activity.

00:22:34.839 --> 00:22:36.839
My frontal lobe is acting as a beacon.

00:22:36.839 --> 00:22:40.839
I've never seen a case this dramatic.

00:22:40.839 --> 00:22:43.839
But we all know that your brain is wired a little differently than the rest of ours.

00:22:43.839 --> 00:22:47.839
Add the fact that the river where she crashed is a known source for our favorite green stuff,

00:22:47.839 --> 00:22:50.839
and you have the perfect Smallville cocktail for weirdness.

00:22:50.839 --> 00:22:53.839
You think the meteor rocks gave her this ability?

00:22:53.839 --> 00:22:56.839
Well, once she's in, she can keep you asleep.

00:22:56.839 --> 00:22:59.839
It certainly explains the day-and-a-half snore-a-thon.

00:22:59.839 --> 00:23:02.839
I didn't wake up until the traveler appeared.

00:23:02.839 --> 00:23:05.839
And I think it's her uncle.

00:23:05.839 --> 00:23:08.839
Or a manifestation of fear that she has for her uncle.

00:23:10.839 --> 00:23:12.839
Sorry. Didn't mean to get all Freudian on you.

00:23:13.839 --> 00:23:15.839
No.

00:23:15.839 --> 00:23:17.839
Her uncle is all-powerful in her life.

00:23:17.839 --> 00:23:19.839
Why wouldn't he be in her dreams?

00:23:19.839 --> 00:23:21.839
You're not buying the altruism angle?

00:23:21.839 --> 00:23:24.839
My faith in human kindness is not what it used to be.

00:23:24.839 --> 00:23:28.839
You up for a trip to the courthouse to see what public records tell us about Uncle Nicholas?

00:23:28.839 --> 00:23:30.839
I have a deadline for the Daily Planet.

00:23:30.839 --> 00:23:33.839
And shockingly, a wall of weird story doesn't take precedence in their mind.

00:23:33.839 --> 00:23:36.839
No time for childish pursuits anymore.

00:23:36.839 --> 00:23:37.839
Hey, now that's not fair.

00:23:37.839 --> 00:23:42.839
You know that if I had a choice, I would definitely be down there pulling dusty records with you.

00:23:42.839 --> 00:23:43.839
I doubt that.

00:23:43.839 --> 00:23:45.839
It's okay, I'll grab Lana.

00:23:45.839 --> 00:23:48.839
Yeah, at least she can provide a constant source of caffeine.

00:24:01.839 --> 00:24:04.839
Now I know why public records are public.

00:24:04.839 --> 00:24:06.839
They're incredibly boring.

00:24:06.839 --> 00:24:07.839
Not all of them.

00:24:07.839 --> 00:24:09.839
Take a look at this.

00:24:10.839 --> 00:24:11.839
Wow.

00:24:11.839 --> 00:24:13.839
Sarah's parents were rich.

00:24:13.839 --> 00:24:15.839
When they died, she inherited everything.

00:24:15.839 --> 00:24:17.839
One guest was in control of the money.

00:24:17.839 --> 00:24:19.839
Uncle Nicholas.

00:24:20.839 --> 00:24:23.839
As long as she stays in a coma, he controls the wealth.

00:24:25.839 --> 00:24:27.839
But he still hasn't done anything wrong.

00:24:27.839 --> 00:24:32.839
I mean, taking care of your niece and living a nice life isn't exactly a smoking gun.

00:24:32.839 --> 00:24:34.839
Then why is Sarah so scared of him?

00:24:35.839 --> 00:24:36.839
I just don't get it.

00:24:36.839 --> 00:24:38.839
Hey, you're tired.

00:24:39.839 --> 00:24:40.839
I'm afraid to close my eyes.

00:24:41.839 --> 00:24:45.799
Uncle put on another pot of coffee.

00:24:48.839 --> 00:24:50.839
You don't have to stay.

00:24:50.839 --> 00:24:53.839
I want to, Clark.

00:24:53.839 --> 00:24:55.839
Sonny?

00:24:55.839 --> 00:24:56.839
Father?

00:24:58.839 --> 00:24:59.839
Come here, Cory.

00:25:02.839 --> 00:25:03.839
Don't clean this room.

00:25:03.839 --> 00:25:04.839
Mother?

00:25:05.839 --> 00:25:06.839
No, hide her.

00:25:06.839 --> 00:25:07.839
Don't you hear?

00:25:07.839 --> 00:25:08.839
Move it in all the room.

00:25:08.839 --> 00:25:09.839
That's his way of moving things.

00:25:09.839 --> 00:25:14.759
That was fast.

00:25:16.899 --> 00:25:17.339
Sarah.

00:25:17.779 --> 00:25:18.099
Hi.

00:25:20.779 --> 00:25:22.099
Must have fallen asleep.

00:25:23.119 --> 00:25:23.559
Yeah.

00:25:24.259 --> 00:25:25.599
How do you get into my dreams?

00:25:27.259 --> 00:25:28.319
I don't know, Clark.

00:25:29.379 --> 00:25:30.879
This has never happened to me before.

00:25:31.839 --> 00:25:34.899
I mean, just the other day, suddenly I was in the woods,

00:25:34.899 --> 00:25:37.439
and then at school, and then at your house.

00:25:37.440 --> 00:25:40.640
I realized what happened when you and Lana came to see me.

00:25:41.500 --> 00:25:42.559
You can hear us?

00:25:44.059 --> 00:25:44.460
Yeah.

00:25:45.480 --> 00:25:47.940
It's like being in a long, dark tunnel.

00:25:48.200 --> 00:25:50.880
I mean, sometimes it's open, but sometimes it's not.

00:25:51.920 --> 00:25:53.279
I tried to reach out to you.

00:25:54.200 --> 00:25:56.400
I mean, you don't know what it's like to be locked in your own body.

00:25:57.140 --> 00:25:58.660
Never any contact.

00:26:01.240 --> 00:26:02.320
Sarah, who's the traveler?

00:26:03.740 --> 00:26:06.180
Oh, we shouldn't talk about him.

00:26:06.480 --> 00:26:07.220
He'll find us.

00:26:07.440 --> 00:26:08.519
He's not even going to be here.

00:26:08.519 --> 00:26:09.559
Is it your uncle?

00:26:11.080 --> 00:26:12.440
Why are you so afraid of him?

00:26:12.440 --> 00:26:13.440
What does he do to you?

00:26:14.400 --> 00:26:15.400
I don't know.

00:26:15.400 --> 00:26:17.400
I used to be able to hear the doctors talking,

00:26:17.400 --> 00:26:19.400
and they said I should have woken up.

00:26:20.460 --> 00:26:22.460
But every time I do feel just a little bit better,

00:26:22.460 --> 00:26:27.460
he does something, and I get sent back to a deep, dark place.

00:26:27.460 --> 00:26:29.460
It's like the bottom of the ocean.

00:26:30.460 --> 00:26:32.200
I almost woke up once.

00:26:32.880 --> 00:26:34.880
That's when he moved us here.

00:26:38.420 --> 00:26:39.500
Oh, God.

00:26:39.539 --> 00:26:40.539
Is he here?

00:26:40.539 --> 00:26:41.539
Yeah.

00:26:43.340 --> 00:26:45.559
Yeah.

00:26:46.440 --> 00:26:49.059
I think he's white in the waves.

00:26:50.559 --> 00:26:52.380
Good.

00:26:52.480 --> 00:26:54.980
Uh, I have a feeling something is going to happen.

00:26:55.279 --> 00:26:57.900
We'll have to see it.

00:26:58.840 --> 00:26:59.900
It won't be long.

00:27:00.880 --> 00:27:01.880
Yes, it will.

00:27:01.880 --> 00:27:02.559
Let's go.

00:27:02.559 --> 00:27:02.940
Go.

00:27:02.940 --> 00:27:03.840
Hey, it's you.

00:27:04.180 --> 00:27:05.240
God, it's you.

00:27:05.240 --> 00:27:06.200
Yeah.

00:27:06.200 --> 00:27:06.519
God.

00:27:06.519 --> 00:27:07.519
You don't believe me?

00:27:07.519 --> 00:27:10.519
I believe you believe it, and that's enough for me.

00:27:10.519 --> 00:27:11.519
You'll have to forgive me, Clark.

00:27:11.519 --> 00:27:14.519
I have a personal bias against psychotherapy.

00:27:14.519 --> 00:27:17.519
You don't like letting people in your head?

00:27:17.519 --> 00:27:18.519
Something like that.

00:27:18.519 --> 00:27:22.519
Well, this girl's in my head until I figure out a way to help her.

00:27:22.519 --> 00:27:24.519
I made a few calls to Metropolis General.

00:27:24.519 --> 00:27:27.519
It's true. Sarah was supposed to wake up.

00:27:27.519 --> 00:27:29.519
So her uncle is drugging her.

00:27:29.519 --> 00:27:31.519
They didn't have any evidence of foul play,

00:27:31.519 --> 00:27:34.519
but they've only performed routine blood tests.

00:27:34.519 --> 00:27:36.519
Maybe he's using a drug that's untraceable.

00:27:36.519 --> 00:27:39.519
Clark, from all appearances, the guy hasn't done anything wrong.

00:27:39.519 --> 00:27:41.519
We both know appearances can be deceiving, Lex.

00:27:41.519 --> 00:27:44.519
Telling the cops you're hurting a dream won't get him arrested.

00:27:44.519 --> 00:27:46.519
I appreciate your help.

00:27:46.519 --> 00:27:48.519
Anytime.

00:27:52.519 --> 00:27:55.519
I've always liked this sword.

00:27:55.519 --> 00:28:00.519
What is it, some sort of legendary samurai antique?

00:28:00.519 --> 00:28:02.519
Hardly. It's a...

00:28:02.519 --> 00:28:04.519
It's a prop from my favorite curfew.

00:28:04.519 --> 00:28:06.519
A Kurosawa movie.

00:28:06.519 --> 00:28:08.519
Throne of Blood.

00:28:08.519 --> 00:28:10.519
I bought it at auction.

00:28:14.519 --> 00:28:17.519
Relax, Clark. It can't hurt you.

00:28:17.519 --> 00:28:19.519
It's not real.

00:28:19.519 --> 00:28:21.519
Right.

00:28:22.519 --> 00:28:25.519
You've got to learn the difference between reality and fantasy.

00:28:27.519 --> 00:28:29.519
Get some sleep.

00:28:34.519 --> 00:28:36.519
Clark.

00:28:36.519 --> 00:28:37.519
Clark.

00:28:37.519 --> 00:28:39.519
This is a pleasant surprise.

00:28:39.519 --> 00:28:42.519
Thought I'd bring Sarah some fresh flowers.

00:28:42.519 --> 00:28:44.519
Come in.

00:28:52.519 --> 00:28:55.519
This is real nice of you, Clark.

00:28:55.519 --> 00:28:58.519
Do you mind if I sit with her for a while?

00:28:58.519 --> 00:29:00.519
Not at all.

00:29:04.519 --> 00:29:06.519
Can I get you something to drink?

00:29:06.519 --> 00:29:08.519
Anything with caffeine.

00:29:08.519 --> 00:29:10.519
I think I might have some soda.

00:29:10.519 --> 00:29:12.519
I think I might have some soda.

00:29:40.519 --> 00:29:42.519
Anything with caffeine?

00:29:42.519 --> 00:29:44.519
I might have some soda if anything else comes up.

00:29:44.519 --> 00:29:45.519
Oh.

00:29:45.519 --> 00:29:46.519
Hey侯

00:29:46.519 --> 00:29:47.519
Hey.

00:29:47.519 --> 00:29:48.519
I should call you-

00:29:48.519 --> 00:29:49.519
Hello?

00:29:49.519 --> 00:29:50.519
Hello?

00:29:51.519 --> 00:29:53.519
Hey.

00:29:53.519 --> 00:29:54.519
When am I looking for you?

00:29:54.519 --> 00:29:55.519
Hey.

00:29:55.519 --> 00:29:58.519
I knew you were looking for me.

00:29:58.519 --> 00:30:00.519
You bought the right dress just now.

00:30:00.519 --> 00:30:02.519
têm you seen me?

00:30:02.519 --> 00:30:03.519
You can go and pick it up one day.

00:30:03.519 --> 00:30:04.519
Sonia, what do you want?

00:30:04.519 --> 00:30:05.519
I'm sorry to pick you up.

00:30:05.519 --> 00:30:06.519
I'm sorry.

00:30:06.519 --> 00:30:07.519
I'm sorry.

00:30:07.519 --> 00:30:08.519
But me too.

00:30:08.519 --> 00:30:09.519
Me too.

00:30:09.519 --> 00:30:10.519
Clark?

00:30:10.519 --> 00:30:11.519
Sarah?

00:30:11.519 --> 00:30:13.519
He's so angry.

00:30:16.519 --> 00:30:19.519
Wait, if you're here, it means I'm...

00:30:39.519 --> 00:30:43.519
Hello?

00:30:43.519 --> 00:30:45.519
Lana, hi. Come on in.

00:30:45.519 --> 00:30:47.519
I was looking for Clark.

00:30:47.519 --> 00:30:49.519
